  "failure_inventory": [
    "Failure inventory before usecase/worker/product implementation:",
    "1. A stale identity hint deletes current live children or quiesces the successor; absent/no-debt work invents completion.",
    "2. Durable Ended alone grants isolation; isolation failure/panic/late completion or changed Owner/UID permits cleanup.",
    "3. Reads accept partial/extra/invalid authority; clock regression, overflow, cancellation or late writes report completion or trigger retry.",
    "4. Cleanup follows newer lifetimes or retries ambiguous writes; partial/conflicting/forged receipts claim completion.",
    "5. Historical coverage is assumed ready; partial/failed/late/panicking build dispatches candidates or monopolizes a turn.",
    "6. Candidate pages admit before whole-page validation; encoded order/terminal cursors/pressure skip work; lost ownership retains unbounded hints.",
    "7. Reclamation uses a second cohort, carries revision/time into dedup keys, starves existing streams or exceeds 256-Slot bounds.",
    "8. Panic/late executor outcome leaks admission or counts confirmation; Stop cannot join and restart overlaps old work.",
    "9. Product composition omits Ender or authoritative index ports; fixed metric labels omit reclamation or retain identifiers.",
    "10. Real cluster autonomous discovery/cleanup does not progress, harms newer lifetime, or destroys source/Will obligations. Full process MQTT acceptance is separately required.",
    "Observed process failure before repair: four zero/offline-expiry scenarios received EOF on reconnect after public reclamation confirmation. Fresh CONNECT reconstructs Session from a zero struct; unlike resume it may drop the persistent reclamation marker required by the lifecycle FSM. A separate three-node Clean Start CONNECT also returned EOF before confirmation; do not infer the same cause without evidence. Add a real acquisition/storage regression across all fresh-lifetime triggers before any repair.",
    "",
    "Captured Clean Start diagnosis: temporary fixed-shape probe recorded phase=commit, definite status=3, expected=3/current=4, old Active generation=1/reclaimed=0. A real normal Disconnect injected before the new lifecycle proposal reproduces both resume and Clean Start rejection. Rebase regressions precede repair: maximum three definite proposals, same isolated Owner/UID/lifetime decision, original candidate and deadline, unknown-write stop, successor protection, freshness-change refusal, cancellation and clock/lease expiry."
  ],
